WEBVTT

00:01.340 --> 00:02.820
<i>Hello there.</i>

00:04.320 --> 00:08.060
<i>It must be late at night,
because things finally calmed down.</i>

00:08.060 --> 00:10.660
<i>But I don't have much to do, 
as there's no one to talk to.</i>

00:10.990 --> 00:14.260
<i>I'll check on my abilities.
I haven't done that in a while.</i>

00:14.260 --> 00:17.660
<i>First, I'll review the different 
types of vending machines.</i>

00:18.000 --> 00:21.230
<i>Vending machines are largely 
divided into two categories:</i>

00:21.230 --> 00:24.350
<i>those that sell goods
and those with automated services.</i>

00:24.350 --> 00:28.500
<i>The first category does exactly what 
it sounds like: they sell products.</i>

00:28.500 --> 00:32.090
<b>Super Draft Taste</b>

00:28.500 --> 00:34.430
<b>Milk for Everybody</b>

00:28.500 --> 00:36.470
<b>Ramune</b>

00:28.920 --> 00:31.480
<i>Even food and drink machines alone 
fall into the subcategories of</i>

00:28.920 --> 00:37.850
<b>Veggie Dietary
 Supplement</b>

00:30.630 --> 00:39.760
<b>Vanilla Lacto
 Ice Cream</b>

00:31.480 --> 00:36.130
<i>soft drinks, coffee, alcohol, milk beverages,
candy, cooking products, and frozen desserts.</i>

00:32.010 --> 00:40.640
<b>Fare Ticket</b>

00:36.090 --> 00:40.930
<b>Revenue Stamp</b>

00:36.130 --> 00:38.510
<i>That leaves cigarettes, tickets, postage 
stamps, postcards, revenue stamps,</i>

00:36.800 --> 00:40.930
<b>Vending Machine News</b>

00:38.510 --> 00:40.920
<i>as well as inspection stamps, 
newspapers, magazines...</i>

00:38.680 --> 00:40.930
<b>Vending Machines</b>

00:42.940 --> 00:44.690
Today's another hot one.

00:43.590 --> 00:44.690
<i>Hello there.</i>

00:46.180 --> 00:47.940
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

00:46.380 --> 00:47.940
Oh, nice and cold.

00:48.770 --> 00:52.440
<i>Next, when it comes to how automated-service 
machines can be categorized,</i>

00:52.440 --> 00:55.380
<i>it's things like money-changing machines 
and pachinko ball dispensers.</i>

00:54.950 --> 00:59.450
<b>Pachinko Ball Dispenser</b>

00:55.380 --> 00:59.440
<i>There's disagreement over recognizing these
automated-service units as vending machines,</i>

00:59.440 --> 01:02.680
<i>but in my opinion they count.</i>

01:02.680 --> 01:06.100
<i>That must be why "power washer" 
is in my function list.</i>

01:06.100 --> 01:07.880
<i>And I only just recently noticed this,</i>

01:07.880 --> 01:10.110
<i>but "rank 3" has been added to that list.</i>

01:10.110 --> 01:13.920
<i>It seems I still have room to 
improve as a vending machine.</i>

01:12.710 --> 01:14.210
<b>Vending Machine Rank-Up</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Investigate</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Sleep</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Conserve Power</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Inspect</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Goods</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Inventory</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Status</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Functions</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Abilities</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Blessings</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Change Paint Color</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Boxed Goods Support</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Vending Machine Security Camera</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Oxygen Vending Machine</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Magazine Vending Machine</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Gas Vending Machine</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Vending Machine Rank-Up;</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Coin-Op Vacuum Cleaner</b>

01:14.210 --> 01:15.220
<b>Kerosene Pump</b>

01:14.310 --> 01:18.080
<i>To attain rank three, I need... 
three million points!</i>

01:15.220 --> 01:16.220
<b>Boxxo</b>

01:15.220 --> 01:16.220
<b>Rank 3</b>

01:16.220 --> 01:18.720
<b>Points needed</b>

01:18.080 --> 01:20.490
<i>I don't even know what it would let me do,</i>

01:18.720 --> 01:21.220
<b>Boxxo</b>

01:18.720 --> 01:21.220
<b>Rank 3</b>

01:20.490 --> 01:24.220
<i>but getting to dream of evolving 
even when I'm a vending machine...</i>

01:25.220 --> 01:27.290
<i>makes me happy beyond...</i>

01:27.720 --> 01:30.770
It's Boxxo! I found him!

01:29.790 --> 01:32.020
You're right! He's over there!

01:32.020 --> 01:32.990
Okay, let's go!

01:32.990 --> 01:36.000
Fright chikin! Fright chikin! Fright chikin!

01:36.220 --> 01:39.670
<i>Yes, it's actually "fried chicken," 
but I can't pronounce it well,</i>

01:39.670 --> 01:42.000
<i>so "fright chikin" is 
what ended up sticking.</i>

01:42.000 --> 01:43.000
<i>Sorry.</i>

01:43.000 --> 01:45.410
Fright chikin!

01:45.410 --> 01:46.510
Give us some!

01:45.990 --> 01:48.990
<i>Calm down already, there's 
plenty to go around!</i>

01:51.090 --> 01:54.000
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

01:56.460 --> 01:58.310
<i>On the outside, a rectangular steel box.</i>

01:58.310 --> 02:00.300
<i>Hidden within is a human soul!</i>

02:00.300 --> 02:05.710
<i>In a world of wonder, I go to and fro 
on the back of my partner Lammis!</i>

02:01.390 --> 02:07.270
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

02:05.710 --> 02:08.150
<i>I am Boxxo! Hello there!</i>

02:08.150 --> 02:09.900
<i>That means "yes"!</i>

03:24.090 --> 03:27.970
<b>Respective Wishes</b>

03:24.610 --> 03:27.710
<i>Hulemy stayed up all night 
fixing the transfer circle,</i>

03:27.710 --> 03:31.080
<i>so we've started evacuating the 
residents of the Origin stratum.</i>

03:31.430 --> 03:34.060
<i>Their place of refuge is the 
Clearflow Lake stratum.</i>

03:34.820 --> 03:39.570
<i>You know, I still don't know how 
many strata this dungeon has.</i>

03:39.570 --> 03:42.870
<i>H-orw m-an-y s-tra-t-a a-re there?</i>

03:42.870 --> 03:45.570
"Horw many"? Oh, how many strata?

03:45.990 --> 03:49.080
From the top, in order, 
there's the Origin stratum,

03:49.380 --> 03:52.570
the Dead's Lament stratum, 
Clearflow Lake stratum,

03:53.020 --> 03:56.080
the Labyrinth stratum, 
Scorching Sand stratum,

03:56.080 --> 03:59.800
Dark Forest stratum,
and then Dog Mountain stratum.

04:00.090 --> 04:03.350
In addition, below that is 
the Everlasting stratum,

04:03.350 --> 04:04.840
which has yet to be conquered.

04:05.190 --> 04:08.620
<i>So at this point, we know there 
are at least eight strata.</i>

04:09.040 --> 04:11.050
Come on, let's begin the evacuation.

04:19.390 --> 04:20.780
Director!

04:21.350 --> 04:22.490
Director!

04:21.910 --> 04:22.710
It's cute!

04:22.710 --> 04:24.190
Thanks!

04:24.190 --> 04:25.370
Director!

04:25.710 --> 04:27.360
Bye-bye!

04:27.360 --> 04:30.100
The transfer circle is working fine.

04:30.100 --> 04:33.100
What will we do regarding it, after this?

04:33.100 --> 04:37.880
If we just abandon it, and the monsters 
misuse it, it'll cause trouble for other strata.

04:37.880 --> 04:40.250
We could resolve that by finding 
the Netherlord's underling

04:40.250 --> 04:43.500
and breaking their control 
over the monsters.

04:43.500 --> 04:48.030
But I can't afford to spare enough 
manpower to go hunting them down.

04:48.030 --> 04:50.910
In that case, how about leaving 
the search exclusively

04:50.910 --> 04:54.010
to the Menagerie of Fools 
and the Band of Gluttons?

04:54.230 --> 04:56.400
<i>There's no point in being all dashing.</i>

04:56.400 --> 04:57.770
You would do that?

04:57.770 --> 04:58.960
I wouldn't mind.

04:58.960 --> 05:02.010
I want more info on the Netherlord anyway.

05:02.010 --> 05:04.780
And it's gonna cost you.

05:05.030 --> 05:08.540
All right. The better the 
results, the higher the reward.

05:09.860 --> 05:12.770
<i>He was going to do it even if she refused.</i>

05:20.500 --> 05:23.140
Mishuel's really got the moves, Aka.

05:23.140 --> 05:25.680
I wish we had a flashy attack, too.

05:31.540 --> 05:34.140
O water, form swirls and pierce!

05:38.070 --> 05:40.910
Well done, everyone.

05:40.910 --> 05:44.250
Boxxo, might I have something to drink?

05:45.740 --> 05:46.990
<b>Kocha Kadan</b>

05:46.990 --> 05:49.980
<i>Your n-o-t f-ight-in?</i>

05:49.980 --> 05:52.770
My primary job is healing.

05:52.770 --> 05:58.420
I possess no offensive magic, so I'm 
basically a bystander during combat.

05:58.420 --> 06:00.370
Put the right people in the right places.

06:00.370 --> 06:02.650
<i>I'm not sure if he's serious or not.</i>

06:02.650 --> 06:05.130
<i>It's hard to read Hevee's face.</i>

06:06.260 --> 06:09.720
<b>Deep within the Origin stratum</b>

06:06.490 --> 06:09.040
Now, which way do we go?

06:09.040 --> 06:13.660
The map says there's a small lake 
not far ahead, to the right.

06:13.660 --> 06:18.760
To the left, it's a long distance,
but there's a three-way split in the path.

06:18.760 --> 06:21.880
I'd like to check out the lake first, but...

06:22.270 --> 06:23.420
What's that?

06:24.300 --> 06:26.910
Great, we can't even pause to talk.

06:29.300 --> 06:32.180
Hevee? It's dangerous to get that close!

06:32.180 --> 06:33.410
Pay it no mind.

06:33.410 --> 06:34.850
H-Hey, Hevee?!

06:34.850 --> 06:36.750
Captain, I'll handle this.

06:36.750 --> 06:38.660
Oh, yeah? Have at it.

06:43.410 --> 06:46.670
<i>What? The enemies keep looking around.</i>

06:46.670 --> 06:49.170
Why aren't the monsters attacking?

06:50.130 --> 06:53.690
I'm just guessing, but they 
probably see invisible walls.

06:53.930 --> 06:57.580
Hevee excels in manipulating 
light to display illusions,

06:57.580 --> 07:02.690
along with abilities that let him 
directly influence the mind.

07:02.980 --> 07:06.150
<i>Oh, like when he hid those 
people in the prison.</i>

07:09.830 --> 07:15.070
I have no interest in those who go barefoot, 
so there's no need to spare these.

07:16.270 --> 07:20.820
He has the Blessing of Might,
but it's not as strong as Lammis's.

07:24.890 --> 07:26.580
<i>Whoa, no mercy!</i>

07:26.580 --> 07:29.840
I figure we can safely leave this to him.

07:36.900 --> 07:39.280
Well, let's split up into two groups.

07:39.280 --> 07:42.140
It wouldn't be very funny if we 
all searched in one direction,

07:42.140 --> 07:44.850
and they got past us by 
coming from the other way.

07:44.850 --> 07:48.630
I shall go with the lake group.

07:48.630 --> 07:50.860
Where should we go, Boxxo?

07:50.860 --> 07:54.230
<i>Hmm, I'm concerned about the 
group that includes Hevee.</i>

07:54.230 --> 07:55.870
<i>If I had to choose...</i>

07:56.280 --> 07:58.120
<b>Megumi Natural Water</b>

07:56.880 --> 07:58.120
<i>Tha-t wa-y.</i>

07:58.120 --> 08:01.040
You want to go to the lake. Sure, okay!

08:01.040 --> 08:03.640
Captain, we're going to the lake.

08:10.260 --> 08:12.830
<i>This search party is only half our members,</i>

08:12.830 --> 08:15.370
<i>but we managed to wipe 
these guys out in no time.</i>

08:15.370 --> 08:17.740
There's the lake! It's so pretty!

08:18.070 --> 08:21.050
We took care of things sooner than expected,

08:21.050 --> 08:23.770
so why don't you all have 
a bit of fun in the water?

08:24.330 --> 08:25.520
<i>That's fishy.</i>

08:25.520 --> 08:28.410
The others are waiting, 
so we need to hurry back.

08:28.640 --> 08:32.660
Well, the captain only said we need 
to be back within three hours.

08:32.660 --> 08:34.610
Yes, that's true.

08:34.610 --> 08:35.540
But...

08:35.540 --> 08:38.530
Okay, I'll go play in the water!

08:38.980 --> 08:40.280
Yeah, I will, too!

08:45.290 --> 08:49.540
<i>Uh-oh, it feels like they're 
this close to joining in.</i>

08:49.540 --> 08:53.700
Ladies, I will be here standing guard.

08:53.700 --> 08:56.410
I think even just dipping your feet 
in the water and washing your hair

08:56.410 --> 08:58.050
will make you feel better.

08:58.050 --> 09:00.710
G-Good point. Want to go, Lammis?

09:00.710 --> 09:03.060
O-Okay, maybe just for a little.

09:03.060 --> 09:05.230
Wait here for a bit, Boxxo!

09:05.230 --> 09:06.930
<i>H-a-v f-u-n.</i>

09:06.930 --> 09:09.540
<i>And form change!</i>

09:09.400 --> 09:10.320
<b>Mr. Pressure</b>

09:10.920 --> 09:14.200
Oh my, this is no place to leave these.

09:14.200 --> 09:16.560
Someone might steal them.

09:16.930 --> 09:19.680
I had better take good care of them.

09:20.340 --> 09:24.110
I wonder what Lammis's and Shui's smell like.

09:24.110 --> 09:25.070
<i>I knew it!</i>

09:25.070 --> 09:26.460
<i>Too bad.</i>

09:29.230 --> 09:31.630
<i>That wasn't hard to see coming at all.</i>

09:31.630 --> 09:34.720
<i>Fully refresh your mind and body in there,</i>

09:34.720 --> 09:37.360
<i>and wash away your worldly 
desires while you're at it.</i>

09:38.670 --> 09:39.930
We're back!

09:39.930 --> 09:41.180
Hi there!

09:41.420 --> 09:43.040
Oh, you're back.

09:43.040 --> 09:45.180
Why is Hevee the only one who's soaked?

09:45.390 --> 09:48.690
I fell in the lake for personal reasons.

09:49.290 --> 09:50.680
Say what?

09:52.610 --> 09:54.950
How about we have lunch?

09:54.950 --> 09:56.660
Boxxo, if you would.

09:56.660 --> 09:58.080
<i>Of course!</i>

09:58.080 --> 10:01.990
<i>I'm thinking of testing out a 
function that's a bit interesting.</i>

10:02.330 --> 10:04.040
<i>Form change!</i>

10:05.050 --> 10:09.200
It's a vending machine store, where you can buy convenience store items 24 hours a day!

10:05.120 --> 10:09.210
<b>Family Market</b>

10:09.200 --> 10:12.960
<i>And I get to show off how I arrange 
things in this limited space.</i>

10:09.210 --> 10:10.460
<b>Rice Ball</b>

10:10.460 --> 10:11.710
<b>Chili Shrimp Fried Rice</b>

10:11.710 --> 10:12.960
<b>Chukadon</b>

10:12.960 --> 10:13.710
<b>Fruit Milk</b>

10:13.420 --> 10:15.810
<i>Okay, so it's the ideal lineup.</i>

10:13.710 --> 10:16.470
<b>Strawberry Milk</b>

10:13.710 --> 10:17.720
<b>Fruit Milk</b>

10:13.710 --> 10:17.720
<b>Yogurt</b>

10:13.710 --> 10:17.720
<b>Cream Puff</b>

10:15.810 --> 10:21.480
<i>Come and relish the power of a vending 
machine turned into a mini convenience store!</i>

10:16.260 --> 10:19.760
<b>Ham Sandwich</b>

10:18.880 --> 10:19.760
<b>Egg Sandwich</b>

10:18.880 --> 10:21.220
<b>Assorted Sandwiches</b>

10:20.220 --> 10:21.220
<b>Rice Ball</b>

10:21.480 --> 10:23.110
<i>Hello there.</i>

10:21.480 --> 10:24.130
Wow, it's a treasure trove!

10:24.130 --> 10:26.990
Oh, there're lots of foods I've never seen!

10:26.210 --> 10:28.490
W-Well, I'll just have to try them all!

10:28.490 --> 10:31.620
I-I will too, from top to bottom!

10:30.640 --> 10:33.520
Calm down, Mikenne! And get down here!

10:32.730 --> 10:35.050
Seriously, it all looks so good.

10:35.050 --> 10:37.220
We're going to have to 
try a number of things.

10:37.220 --> 10:38.520
Which should we have, Aka?

10:38.520 --> 10:41.480
Shiro, let's each choose different items,
and go halfsies!

10:41.770 --> 10:43.640
What's this? How does it work?

10:43.430 --> 10:44.500
<i>Oh, right.</i>

10:43.640 --> 10:45.380
Calm down, Mikenne!

10:44.500 --> 10:48.860
<i>They probably don't know how to open 
a rice ball, so I should demonstrate.</i>

10:45.160 --> 10:49.500
<b>Plum Rice Ball</b>

10:45.380 --> 10:48.270
First you do this, then that... Huh?

10:50.500 --> 10:52.240
What's that, Boxxo?!

10:54.860 --> 10:56.730
Um, everyone!

10:57.870 --> 10:59.670
I apologize...

11:00.410 --> 11:02.340
But could someone...

11:02.340 --> 11:03.560
Take this!

11:03.560 --> 11:06.010
...take my place now?!

11:06.410 --> 11:07.460
Boxxo.

11:07.240 --> 11:08.190
Boxxo.

11:07.930 --> 11:10.020
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
 I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

11:08.170 --> 11:09.380
Boxxo.

11:12.980 --> 11:14.020
Halt.

11:14.020 --> 11:17.020
We'll probably find them 
somewhere down this hill.

11:17.020 --> 11:18.440
Yes, most likely.

11:17.030 --> 11:20.490
<b>Deepest part of the Origin stratum</b>

11:18.440 --> 11:21.780
Mishuel, can you sense how 
many beings are down there?

11:23.290 --> 11:26.170
They're too close together 
for me to be accurate.

11:26.170 --> 11:29.300
We should be prepared 
for at least a hundred.

11:29.300 --> 11:30.650
Is that all?

11:30.650 --> 11:33.840
Then there's not much chance of us getting 
hammered even if our front line charges in.

11:33.840 --> 11:35.970
Mishuel and I will take the lead.

11:35.970 --> 11:37.550
That is fine by me.

11:37.830 --> 11:40.170
<i>Is there anything I can do?</i>

11:40.170 --> 11:42.860
<i>Like, some way to slow down the monsters?</i>

11:43.380 --> 11:44.940
<i>I could always use that!</i>

11:44.940 --> 11:46.420
<i>Form change!</i>

11:47.520 --> 11:49.680
Boxxo? What's up?

11:50.850 --> 11:52.580
<i>M-oo-v a-s-igh-d.</i>

11:51.390 --> 11:52.560
<b>Pachinko Ball Dispenser</b>

11:55.560 --> 11:57.800
This is kind of incredible.

12:00.650 --> 12:03.250
Master Boxxo, what are these balls?

12:03.250 --> 12:04.730
<i>You're too close, too close.</i>

12:04.730 --> 12:06.620
<i>M-oo-v t-r-i-p.</i>

12:07.200 --> 12:11.600
Um, if they move, the balls 
will make them trip and fall?

12:11.600 --> 12:12.700
<i>C-or-e-c-t.</i>

12:12.990 --> 12:16.460
<i>We should declare Lammis a 
first-class Boxxo interpreter!</i>

12:17.970 --> 12:20.560
I think I hear monsters 
screaming from down that way.

12:20.560 --> 12:22.840
They sound weird, and there's lots of noise.

12:22.840 --> 12:25.840
Good, Boxxo's set the stage for us.

12:25.840 --> 12:27.240
Let's get in there!

12:27.240 --> 12:28.100
Yes, sir!

12:28.830 --> 12:33.270
If there's this many of them, it's a 
safe bet there's a commander here!

12:33.270 --> 12:34.410
Heading in!

12:34.410 --> 12:35.870
Roaring Strike!

12:38.980 --> 12:44.660
Wow. If I could get that strong, 
I'd be of more help to everyone.

12:48.030 --> 12:49.630
<i>You're fine, Lammis.</i>

12:49.620 --> 12:53.290
<b>Kocha Kadan</b>

12:49.620 --> 12:53.290
<b>Early Afternoon Tea</b>

12:49.630 --> 12:52.020
<i>And I'd better get busy, too!</i>

12:52.020 --> 12:55.100
<i>Recently, I realized I can switch out 
goods to get access to this candy,</i>

12:55.100 --> 12:57.950
<i>without turning into the 
specialized vending machine.</i>

12:57.950 --> 13:00.380
<i>You never know these things unless you try.</i>

13:00.690 --> 13:02.040
<i>Launch!</i>

13:06.800 --> 13:09.840
Boxxo, can you handle the enemies behind us?

13:09.840 --> 13:11.050
<i>Hello there.</i>

13:11.260 --> 13:14.290
<i>Letting me cover her back is 
proof that she trusts me!</i>

13:14.290 --> 13:16.310
<i>It's a man's job to live up to that!</i>

13:16.670 --> 13:19.820
<i>I know now that this works 
great as a blunt weapon,</i>

13:19.820 --> 13:24.330
<i>so I'll take on any enemy that tries 
to attack Lammis from behind!</i>

13:24.560 --> 13:26.290
Roaring Strike!

13:30.700 --> 13:32.090
They just keep coming.

13:32.360 --> 13:35.320
<i>We can't win if new ones show 
up as fast as we defeat them.</i>

13:35.320 --> 13:37.960
<i>We need to locate the commander somehow.</i>

13:37.960 --> 13:40.200
<i>I might as well try asking her.</i>

13:40.200 --> 13:41.300
<i>L-a-i-s.</i>

13:41.300 --> 13:42.040
You called?

13:43.410 --> 13:45.670
<i>T-o-s m-ea o-ver there.</i>

13:46.170 --> 13:48.740
You want me to throw you over there?

13:49.530 --> 13:50.470
No!

13:50.470 --> 13:52.800
I don't want to use you like a tool!

13:52.800 --> 13:54.410
<i>Your p-ert-n-er.</i>

13:54.410 --> 13:55.940
"Pertner"?

13:57.930 --> 13:59.940
Yeah, we're partners.

13:59.940 --> 14:02.100
And let me say this, as your partner.

14:02.520 --> 14:03.700
Nope!

14:03.700 --> 14:04.690
<i>Oo.</i>

14:04.690 --> 14:09.340
Boxxo, you're trying to put yourself 
in harm's way out of concern for me.

14:09.340 --> 14:11.530
But it's the same for me.

14:11.530 --> 14:14.460
I don't want you to get hurt either!

14:14.460 --> 14:16.710
<i>Yeah... You're right.</i>

14:16.710 --> 14:17.960
<i>S-or-ry.</i>

14:17.960 --> 14:19.890
No need to apologize.

14:19.890 --> 14:21.860
Our two hearts beat as one.

14:21.860 --> 14:24.090
I attack, you defend!

14:24.090 --> 14:25.810
The two of us can do anything!

14:25.810 --> 14:26.460
<i>Y-ea.</i>

14:26.760 --> 14:31.480
<i>From now on we'll work together, 
and discuss a sure way to—</i>

14:31.480 --> 14:34.970
And so, let's <i>both</i> launch a suicide attack!

14:34.970 --> 14:36.410
<i>W-Wait a minute, miss?</i>

14:36.410 --> 14:39.230
<i>Don't you think that's rather extreme?!</i>

14:39.230 --> 14:41.610
<i>O-o-o-o-o.</i>

14:40.770 --> 14:42.570
Lammis? Master Boxxo?

14:42.570 --> 14:44.830
U-Um, I'll clear a path!

14:46.630 --> 14:48.840
Master Boxxo! Feel free to proceed!

14:49.050 --> 14:51.400
<i>No, no! Feel free to stop us!</i>

14:51.400 --> 14:52.910
Thanks, Mishuel!

14:52.910 --> 14:54.890
That's Boxxo's #1 apprentice for you!

14:54.890 --> 14:57.150
Oh, not at all.

14:57.150 --> 14:59.670
<i>Mishuel seems pleased by the compliment!</i>

14:59.670 --> 15:01.660
<i>Urgh, here goes nothing!</i>

15:05.830 --> 15:08.700
<i>To incapacitate enemies 
without defeating them...</i>

15:08.700 --> 15:10.380
<i>That calls for pachinko balls!</i>

15:10.380 --> 15:14.130
<i>The best product for slipping and 
falling would have to be these!</i>

15:14.130 --> 15:15.300
<i>Launch!</i>

15:20.180 --> 15:21.890
<i>Oh, this is entertaining!</i>

15:21.890 --> 15:22.950
<i>I'll keep adding more!</i>

15:28.390 --> 15:29.960
<i>That takes care of them.</i>

15:29.960 --> 15:32.290
Boxxo, where's the commander?

15:32.290 --> 15:35.950
<i>It's all green fiends. I don't see 
anything that looks like a commander.</i>

15:35.950 --> 15:37.160
Boxxo!

15:38.150 --> 15:39.440
What're these?!

15:44.440 --> 15:46.820
Mikenne! You okay? What happened?

15:45.490 --> 15:48.490
Whew, safe. Thanks.

15:48.490 --> 15:52.730
Listen, earlier, I heard what sounded 
like human screams from over there.

15:52.730 --> 15:55.100
I think it was inside that mound.

15:55.100 --> 15:57.440
There're still faint moans coming out.

15:57.440 --> 16:00.620
<i>Ah, that first attack 
must have done the job!</i>

16:00.620 --> 16:03.650
<i>In that case, form change!</i>

16:03.560 --> 16:04.440
<b>Refreshing</b>

16:03.560 --> 16:04.440
<b>Coin-Op
Power Washer</b>

16:03.560 --> 16:04.440
<b>Osugi Cleaning Factory</b>

16:03.560 --> 16:04.440
<b>Mr. Pressure</b>

16:03.650 --> 16:05.750
<i>Power washer!</i>

16:07.940 --> 16:09.430
They're in there, huh?

16:09.430 --> 16:11.800
Okay, I'll go look. Wait here!

16:11.800 --> 16:12.700
Good luck.

16:17.910 --> 16:18.710
<i>There!</i>

16:20.200 --> 16:21.930
That must be the commander!

16:24.050 --> 16:27.610
When the adversary can't stop them,
you go for the ring.

16:30.960 --> 16:32.720
That's one less thing to worry about!

16:33.410 --> 16:35.000
<i>L-ext l-ea-v.</i>

16:35.000 --> 16:36.090
Master Boxxo!

16:36.090 --> 16:37.630
We opened up a retreat path!

16:37.630 --> 16:39.860
Fall back to the pathway!

16:40.540 --> 16:44.310
Now that we've made it back this far,
it's mission accomplished.

16:44.310 --> 16:47.360
I guess we'll question girlie here 
once we get back to the village.

16:47.360 --> 16:48.440
Yes, we will.

16:48.440 --> 16:52.940
But should you be taking advantage of this 
hectic situation to pat a woman's rear?

16:52.190 --> 16:54.970
W-Well, I was just caught up in the moment.

16:54.970 --> 16:57.060
It wasn't like I was planning 
on touching her there.

16:57.060 --> 16:58.260
Oh, really?

16:58.260 --> 17:00.450
Those two are so good together.

17:00.450 --> 17:01.610
<i>Y-ea ry-l-y.</i>

17:01.860 --> 17:04.620
<i>What exactly is their relationship, anyway?</i>

17:03.630 --> 17:06.720
Captain, you always act like this.

17:05.790 --> 17:09.490
These two should be old 
enough to know better, Aka.

17:06.720 --> 17:09.490
As vice captain, I must say, 
it sets a bad example.

17:09.490 --> 17:12.520
Hey, come on. I'm, like, 
not into butts at all.

17:09.490 --> 17:12.790
I'll say. It's always embarrassing to watch.

17:12.790 --> 17:14.490
They're "old enough"?

17:14.490 --> 17:16.890
Isn't Vice Captain Filmina young?

17:16.890 --> 17:18.610
Oh, you didn't know?

17:18.610 --> 17:21.670
She might not look it,
but she's older than the captain.

17:21.670 --> 17:23.730
Wh-What? But she's so young!

17:23.730 --> 17:28.520
Um, the vice captain is half... 
some race I can't remember.

17:28.520 --> 17:30.520
Vamp fiend, Shui.

17:30.520 --> 17:33.520
<i>Vamp fiend? I've never heard of that race.</i>

17:33.520 --> 17:39.040
Um, isn't that a race that 
feeds on people's blood?

17:39.040 --> 17:41.520
They're all beautiful people 
who look just like humans.

17:41.520 --> 17:45.110
To add to that, I hear vamp 
fiends can also get nourishment

17:41.540 --> 17:54.800
<b>Kocha Kadan</b>

17:45.110 --> 17:48.500
from bodily fluids where the 
composition is similar to blood.

17:49.660 --> 17:53.660
Which is why it isn't uncommon for them 
to bond with humans and have children.

17:53.660 --> 17:54.810
I do believe.

17:55.090 --> 17:59.090
That sounds lovely, like destiny!

17:59.090 --> 18:01.190
That doesn't bother you at all, Lammis?

18:01.190 --> 18:03.500
You know, it means doing 
<i>that</i> with a monster.

18:03.500 --> 18:05.310
Many consider it an abomination.

18:05.610 --> 18:08.320
<i>Looks like Lammis's reaction 
came as a surprise.</i>

18:08.320 --> 18:11.140
But even if someone's race 
or appearance is different,

18:11.140 --> 18:14.160
it doesn't change them as 
a person, so I don't mind!

18:14.160 --> 18:15.380
Right, Boxxo?

18:15.380 --> 18:16.700
<i>Y-ea, y-ea.</i>

18:16.700 --> 18:19.560
And the Menagerie of Fools has accepted her.

18:19.560 --> 18:21.880
So, she's just the same as everyone else.

18:21.880 --> 18:25.030
Well, we're all a bunch of oddballs.

18:26.280 --> 18:31.330
I just remembered, I heard the Menagerie 
of Fools has wishes they want granted.

18:31.330 --> 18:34.080
Is it okay for me to ask what all they are?

18:37.090 --> 18:40.150
S-Sorry. There are things people 
don't want to talk about.

18:40.150 --> 18:41.550
It's okay.

18:41.550 --> 18:46.220
I only have one wish—to get lots of money 
and make things easier for the orphanage,

18:46.220 --> 18:51.240
so the children and I can eat all the 
tasty food we want every day together!

18:47.230 --> 18:51.230
<b>Egg Sandwich</b>

18:51.240 --> 18:54.160
<i>Yeah, that's a simple, Shui kind of wish.</i>

18:54.480 --> 18:56.730
Okay, I'll say mine next.

18:56.730 --> 19:00.010
My wish is to make Boxxo human again.

19:00.010 --> 19:04.120
Does that mean you two have the same wish?

19:04.120 --> 19:04.740
<i>Y-ea.</i>

19:04.980 --> 19:08.000
<i>I have a lot of them,
 but let's leave it at that.</i>

19:08.000 --> 19:11.750
Well then, I shall confess my own wish.

19:11.750 --> 19:13.250
Hard pass, Hevee.

19:14.070 --> 19:18.630
Oh, no. To hear everyone else's 
desire while I keep mine to myself

19:18.630 --> 19:21.010
would be conduct unbecoming of a person.

19:21.450 --> 19:26.010
My wish is to collect footwear from all 
over the world just before it wears out,

19:26.010 --> 19:29.510
and use it to construct a great castle.

19:29.510 --> 19:34.430
I have a dream on a grand scale, 
where once a year I receive, as a tax,

19:34.430 --> 19:37.200
footwear that's been worn 
throughout the previous year.

19:37.860 --> 19:41.110
<i>That really is a shameful wish.</i>

19:42.360 --> 19:44.470
I guess it's our turn next.

19:44.470 --> 19:46.230
I too share a wish with Shiro.

19:46.230 --> 19:47.120
Right?

19:47.120 --> 19:48.190
That's right, Aka.

19:48.190 --> 19:50.320
Our wish is...

19:50.320 --> 19:53.290
...to be popular with the ladies!

19:53.630 --> 19:56.390
That's rich, coming from 
a couple of virgins.

19:58.280 --> 19:59.370
<i>Too bad.</i>

19:59.370 --> 20:01.370
What about the captain and vice captain?

20:01.370 --> 20:03.120
That I don't know.

20:03.120 --> 20:06.640
I asked them about it once, 
but they dodged the question.

20:06.850 --> 20:07.900
Same here.

20:07.900 --> 20:08.890
Same here.

20:09.170 --> 20:11.900
Every person has their secrets.

20:11.900 --> 20:14.600
There's no need to try to ferret them out.

20:14.850 --> 20:18.600
<i>Hevee has good things to say, 
when it's not about shoes.</i>

20:19.250 --> 20:21.280
Hurry it up, you guys!

20:21.280 --> 20:23.610
Or we won't make it back 
to the village today.

20:23.610 --> 20:25.540
Okay!

20:26.110 --> 20:28.130
Well done, all of you!

20:28.400 --> 20:32.770
Boxxo, may I trouble you to provide 
food and drinks for a feast?

20:32.770 --> 20:34.120
<i>Hello there.</i>

20:34.120 --> 20:35.960
<b>Super Ice</b>

20:35.650 --> 20:37.650
Looks good!

20:38.910 --> 20:40.040
Been waiting for this!

20:40.040 --> 20:41.260
I'm so happy!

20:40.410 --> 20:42.140
<i>Fright chikin, fright chikin!</i>

20:42.140 --> 20:43.550
Yes!

20:43.820 --> 20:48.300
<i>All right, now to try out something 
I've been wanting to try.</i>

20:48.300 --> 20:50.140
<i>Form change!</i>

20:49.310 --> 20:52.060
<b>Koshihikari
No-Wash Rice</b>

20:50.140 --> 20:52.070
<i>A rice vending machine!</i>

20:52.400 --> 20:57.560
<i>Now that I have Telekinesis, I can 
even prepare it myself... I think.</i>

20:57.560 --> 20:59.610
<i>Now, how will I cook this?</i>

20:59.610 --> 21:01.890
Hey Boxxo, what's this?

21:01.890 --> 21:03.320
It's cookery, right?

21:03.320 --> 21:04.440
<i>I know!</i>

21:04.440 --> 21:08.450
Koshihikari
No-Wash Rice

21:04.440 --> 21:08.460
<i>C-ook-in, please hel-p.</i>

21:08.460 --> 21:09.820
Okay, sure.

21:08.460 --> 21:11.030
What should we do?

21:11.030 --> 21:12.450
<i>Form change!</i>

21:12.450 --> 21:14.770
<i>A gas vending machine!</i>

21:13.540 --> 21:15.960
<b>Gas Vending Machine</b>

21:14.770 --> 21:15.950
<i>Pl-a-s o-n.</i>

21:15.950 --> 21:17.280
Like this?

21:17.280 --> 21:18.350
<i>Thank you.</i>

21:18.650 --> 21:21.460
Oh, this is a magic item that produces fire.

21:21.460 --> 21:26.240
<i>I did get some help at the end,
but I think I can handle simple cooking.</i>

21:26.240 --> 21:29.900
But Boxxo, why'd you start 
cooking all of a sudden?

21:29.900 --> 21:31.520
That's a good question.

21:31.520 --> 21:33.720
You can already dispense all kinds of foods.

21:34.980 --> 21:38.280
<i>It would be hard to say I 
just tried it for kicks.</i>

21:39.800 --> 21:41.910
<i>This rice is done!</i>

21:41.910 --> 21:43.590
I'll go get bowls!

21:43.590 --> 21:44.960
I'll help, too.

21:46.510 --> 21:48.320
This is good!

21:48.320 --> 21:49.740
Yeah, it's tasty!

21:51.530 --> 21:57.240
<i>All I did was cook using my own abilities, 
but I'm surprisingly happy right now.</i>

21:57.640 --> 22:00.500
Boxxo, thanks for all you do.

22:01.330 --> 22:04.110
<i>I think I might cook again, 
from time to time!</i>

23:35.060 --> 23:37.040
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.050
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.050
<b>Sweet Temptation</b>

23:37.990 --> 23:40.170
<i>I look forward to your next use.</i>
